<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-22">22 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bloody Sunday in St Petersburg sparks revolution</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Imperial troops fired on unarmed workers led by Father Georgy Gapon marching to petition <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a>, killing many. The massacre set off the 1905 Revolution and badly damaged faith in the Tsar.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-26">26 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Cullinan diamond, the largest ever found, discovered</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Mine manager Frederick <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">Wells</a> found a 3,106-carat rough diamond at the Premier Mine near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a>. Cut into nine major stones, it supplied the largest gems in the British Crown Jewels.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-23">23 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rotary Club founded in Chicago</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Lawyer Paul Harris and three business acquaintances met to found the first Rotary Club. Rotary International now has some 1.4 million members and led the campaign to eradicate polio.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-17">17 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Einstein completes his paper on light quanta</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Einstein finished a paper proposing that light comes in discrete packets of energy, explaining the photoelectric effect. It helped found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quantum-mechanics">quantum theory</a> and earned him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-7">7 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Norway dissolves its union with Sweden</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Norwegian parliament declared that King Oscar II had ceased to rule as King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> accepted the separation peacefully after a referendum, and Norway chose a Danish prince as king.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-27">27 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sailors mutiny aboard the battleship Potemkin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Crew of the Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea-fleet">Black Sea Fleet</a> battleship rose against their officers after a dispute over rotten meat. The mutiny became a symbol of the 1905 Revolution, later immortalised by Eisenstein.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-30">30 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Einstein's paper on special relativity reaches the journal</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Annalen der Physik received 'On the Electrodynamics of Moving Bodies', which showed that measurements of time and space depend on motion. E = mc² followed in a short sequel that autumn.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-30">30 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ty Cobb makes his major league debut</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Eighteen-year-old Ty Cobb hit a double in his first game for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a> Tigers. His lifetime batting average of .366 remains the highest in major league history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-26">26 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Einstein's paper on special relativity is published</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Annalen der Physik published Einstein's 'On the Electrodynamics of Moving Bodies', which showed that measurements of time and space depend on the observer's motion. It transformed physics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-28">28 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Arthur Griffith launches Sinn Féin's policy</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At a convention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, Arthur Griffith set out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinn-fein">Sinn Féin</a> policy, meaning 'we ourselves', of Irish self-reliance and a separate Irish parliament. The movement later became central to the struggle for independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Russo-Japanese War was a conflict between the Russian Empire and the Empire of Japan over influence in Manchuria and Korea, concluded by the Treaty of Portsmouth in 1905.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution-of-1905">Russian Revolution of 1905</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Russian Revolution of 1905 was a wave of strikes, peasant uprisings, mutinies and political protest across the Russian Empire, sparked by the Bloody Sunday massacre in Saint Petersburg and defeat in the war with Japan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-portsmouth" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-portsmouth.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-portsmouth">Treaty of Portsmouth</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Portsmouth ended the Russo-Japanese War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/japan-korea-treaty-of-1905" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/japan-korea-treaty-of-1905.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/japan-korea-treaty-of-1905">Japan–Korea Treaty of 1905</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Japan–Korea Treaty of 1905, known in Korea as the Eulsa Treaty, was signed on 17 November 1905 after the Russo-Japanese War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tsushima" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tsushima.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tsushima">Battle of Tsushima</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tsushima was a naval battle fought in May 1905 in the strait between Korea and Japan, the decisive engagement of the Russo-Japanese War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/karlstad-convention">Karlstad Convention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Karlstad Convention was the set of agreements negotiated at Karlstad, Sweden, in September 1905 that settled the peaceful dissolution of the union between Sweden and Norway.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/theriso-revolt" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theriso-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/theriso-revolt">Theriso revolt</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Theriso revolt was an uprising in the Cretan State in 1905, led by Eleftherios Venizelos from the village of Theriso near Chania.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/moravian-compromise">Moravian Compromise</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Moravian Compromise was a set of laws adopted in 1905 that reorganised the Moravian Diet and its electoral system along national lines.</p></div></li></ol></section>
