<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/empire-of-japan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empire%20of%20Japan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empire of Japan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Admiral Togo annihilates the Russian fleet at Tsushima, sealing victory over Russia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Defeat at Tsushima and revolution force Nicholas II to issue the October Manifesto</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Norway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Norway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The union with Sweden is dissolved and Haakon VII becomes king</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rattanakosin-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rattanakosin%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rattanakosin Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Slave Abolition Act completes the end of slavery</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/barotseland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Barotseland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Barotseland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Italian arbitration fixes the border with Angola, cutting off western lands</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/confucianism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Confucianism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Confucianism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Qing government abolishes the imperial examinations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/indian-independence-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indian%20independence%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indian independence movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lord Curzon’s partition of Bengal provokes the Swadeshi movement and the boycott of British goods</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/absolute-monarchy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Absolute%20monarchy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Absolute monarchy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nicholas II’s October Manifesto promises Russia an elected Duma, ending unlimited autocracy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/caral-supe-civilisation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Caral%E2%80%93Supe%20civilisation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Caral–Supe civilisation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Max Uhle notes the site of Caral, though he does not recognise its hills as pyramids</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-third-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Third%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Third Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The law on the separation of Church and State abolishes Napoleon's Concordat of 1801</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/sun-yat-sen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sun%20Yat-sen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sun Yat-sen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He forms the Tongmenghui with Chinese students in Tokyo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-east-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20East%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German East Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Governor Gustav Adolf von Götzen crushes the Maji Maji Rebellion by measures to create a famine, which may have cost as many as 300,000 lives</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 27 May the Japanese auxiliary cruiser Shinano Maru sights the Russian fleet and wireless reports reach Tōgō on the Mikasa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the afternoon of 27 May Tōgō turns his line in sequence in the afternoon, Oslyabya, Knyaz Suvorov, Imperator Aleksandr III and Borodino are lost, and Rozhestvensky is knocked unconscious</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">From about 20:00 Japanese destroyers and torpedo boats attack the scattered Russian ships through the night</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 28 May Nebogatov surrenders his remaining battleships and Tōgō accepts after the signal flags are understood</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Portsmouth ends the war</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tsushima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tsushima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tsushima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain begins construction of HMS Dreadnought</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/kebra-nagast"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kebra%20Nagast.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kebra Nagast</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Carl Bezold publishes the entire text with commentary</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/arthashastra"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Arthashastra.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Arthashastra</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A palm-leaf manuscript given to the Mysore Oriental Library is identified by Rudrapatna Shamasastry as the Arthashastra</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/golden-temple"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Golden%20Temple.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Golden Temple</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Idols and images were removed from the Golden Temple after the campaign of the Tat Khalsa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/albert-einstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Albert%20Einstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Albert Einstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Publishes four papers on the photoelectric effect, Brownian motion, special relativity and the equivalence of mass and energy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/empress-dowager-cixi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empress%20Dowager%20Cixi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empress Dowager Cixi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The examination system is abolished among the reforms of the New Policies</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/persian-constitutional-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Persian%20Constitutional%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Persian Constitutional Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Merchants and clergy protest against tariffs imposed to repay the Russian loan for the shah's tour of Europe</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/jadidism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jadidism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jadidism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 1905 Revolution opens a period in which Turkic-language newspapers appear in Turkestan; Russian authorities forbid them again in 1908</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/hundred-days-reform"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hundred%20Days'%20Reform.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hundred Days' Reform</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The imperial examination is abolished, one of the late Qing reforms that followed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/trotskyism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Trotskyism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Trotskyism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Trotsky chairs the St. Petersburg Soviet and formulates the theory of permanent revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/secularism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Secularism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Secularism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A French law enshrines laïcité, the principle of strict separation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/three-principles-of-the-people"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Three%20Principles%20of%20the%20People.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Three Principles of the People</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sun first sets out the ideas behind his Principles in a speech in Brussels, and the Tongmenghui is formed in Tokyo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/syndicalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Syndicalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Syndicalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Industrial Workers of the World is founded in the United States</span></li></ul></section>
